      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T17:47:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would prefer that all the assignments conditional on UARTN were bunched together at the top of the file, so that we have only one #if (UARTN \u003d\u003d 0) directive.\n\n#if (UARTN \u003d\u003d 0)\n#define MXC_UART MXC_UART0\n#define EC_UART_IRQn EC_UART0_IRQn\n#elif (UARTN \u003d\u003d 1)\n#define MXC_UART MXC_UART1\n#define EC_UART_IRQn EC_UART1_IRQn\n#else\n#error \"MAX32660 supports only UART 0 or 1 for EC console\"\n#endif\n\n...\n\n        MXC_UART-\u003ectrl \u003d ....\n\nThe compiler may optimize mxc_uart_regs_t *uart away, saving stack space in the current code, but with the define instead, we are sure that it will not waste stack space.",
